clean_summary:
Marin is the most open model training initiative in the world. It allows visualization of the exact pre-training mixture per domain, sampling documents, monitoring live training loss, examining configs, and understanding scaling laws.

@percyliang: "Marin 535B-A23B started training this week! As usual, the whole process is open. The voyage plan includes pretraining (80%) and midtraining (20%) on 18.75T tokens using 11 NVL72 GPUs for about three months, totaling 2.7e24 FLOPs. Post-training will follow."

Before the main run, a scaling ladder from 1.6B to 27.7B parameters was trained on varying token counts to debug issues and forecast the main run. This is the largest run so far, so unexpected results are anticipated."

So happy for the whole Marin team. They've been quietly working up to this for a long time. I'm excited to get to work with the community post-training this model.

@percyliang: "Marin 535B-A23B started training this week! As usual, the whole process is open. Voyage plan: pretraining (80%) plus midtraining (20%) on 18.75T tokens across 11 NVL72 GPUs for about 3 months. Post-training will follow."

Before starting the main run, they trained a 4-rung scaling ladder from 1.6B-A61M (48B tokens) to 27.7B-A1.2B (926B tokens) to debug issues and forecast the main run. This is their biggest project yet, so surprises are expected.
